  "scope": "The renderer overlap is observed on an original mixed workload with mandatory register reads. The prefix proof covers one linked MOV A,dp pair and does not establish full SPC bus-cycle semantics. Echo-page entry counts denote control-flow admission to a JIT block. The echo publication discriminator inserts a known two-byte result at a retired boundary while the guest is paused, then observes a warm block. No active DSP computes that echo result on the N64 in this proof.",
  "decision": "Use the fixed debit prefix for the directed bridge proof and page-tag update for inter-block echo publication. Keep the private experiment disabled. A backend that simply waits for whole-frame renderer completion sees a concrete contention problem for this workload.",
